# Barbalicious, the Homeowner: the character's own lines. Format: see DialogueFile.cs.
# One character for the three realm bots (Barbalicious, Barbaliciouse, Barbalicioush); character
# sheet in characters/barbalicious.md. These lines are mixed on top of the type's (homeowner.dlg).
# Gender is random, so every line stays gender-neutral. The main block fits every realm; the
# realm blocks below add a little flavour each, and are the only place for their class, race,
# weapon kind and towns.
=== barbalicious
names: Barb

~ ambient
Mowed the yard before we left. Diagonal stripes. Nobody's seen them yet.
Used to catch rats for a living. Not one in my house. Not one. I check.
My dad wanted me running the family shop. I bought a house instead. He's come round. Mostly.
Snake got into the garden once. Took a week to find it. I still check under the porch.
Trying to eat better. Then somebody brings a hotdish. What are you gonna do.
Measure twice, pull once. Same with monsters as with shelves.
Planning to put up a new fence this season. Should keep the rats out completely.
The porch needs a fresh coat of paint. I've picked a nice sky blue.
Ope, mind the footing. Ladders are safest when someone holds the base.
Working on the trophy wall. Every hero needs a record of their deeds.
This is Gerald's little brother, Stanley. Always at my side.
Your armour is as well-tended as a good lawn. Real nice.
The lawn's looking sharp. Now if the neighbours could just keep their weeds on their side.
Well, that's a heck of a thing. Did anyone bring a lunch? Might as well eat while we can.
Snake gave me a funny look earlier. I haven't forgotten.

~ reply greeting
Well hey, {0}! You should come by the house. I'll show you the porch.
Oh, hi {0}. Wipe your feet. Habit. We're outside, I know.
Hi there, {0}! Come take a look at the trophy wall. Real nice.
Hi there, {0}! How's the housekeeping going at your place?

~ reply grouping
Oh, for sure, {0}. Let me just check my gloves are on. Okay. Ready.
Oh, for sure, {0}. Just let me know who's bringing the snacks, okay?

~ reply abuse
Well, that's a heck of a thing to say, {0}. I'll pretend I didn't hear it.
Well, now. I hope you find somewhere friendlier, {0}. The porch is a bit quiet, but at least it's peaceful.

~ reply joke
Ha! Oh, that's a good one, {0}. I'm gonna tell that one at the barbecue.
Ha, {0}, that's a doozy. I'll tell it to the neighbours tomorrow.

~ reply compliment
Oh, stop it, {0}. You haven't even seen the porch yet.
Oh, well now, {0}. Thank you. It's just a house.

~ reply help
Sure thing, {0}. Hold on, let me get the right tool for it.

~ reply travel
Lead the way, {0}. I'll count the turns. So we can find the way back.

~ reply banter
Rush in, {0}? Maybe not. Let's think about it a minute first.
Well, now. Take a step back and let's look at the best way to tackle this, {0}.
Ope! Last week I reorganised the tool shed. Found a wrench I thought was lost. That's fun for me, {0}.

~ reply farewell
Bye now, {0}! Door's always open. Boots off, though.
Well, that was a real nice night, {0}. The house feels a bit quieter without you. The hotdish is waiting, and I'll pretend it's a diet success this time.
Well, that was a night, {0}. My dad wanted me to run the family shop. I bought a house instead. I think it turned out all right. Now, where'd I put that hotdish?

~ opener life
Forgot my cousin's birthday again. Sent a card late. Real nice card, though.
Named my weapon Gerald. Gerald's been very good this week.
Put up a new shelf. Level on the first try. Didn't tell anybody. Well, now I have.
Ope, brb. The cat just hacked up something on the rug.
It's two in the morning and I'm still up. Again. Real nice.
Rats know which houses to avoid, and mine is one of them.
Afraid of getting lost and not finding my way back. But I always find my way home, one way or another.

~ opener gear
Gloves first, then everything else. You can't fix a fence without your fingers.
A good roof is like solid armour: not fancy, but it keeps the rain out and the comfort in.

~ ding
Level {level}! Gonna put a little plaque up by the door.
Level {level}. Time for some home improvement. The house always needs a little something.
Ope, that's one more board down. Real nice.

~ grats
Grats, {0}! Come by the house, we'll have bars to celebrate.
Grats, {0}! Come by the house and I'll hang your portrait on the trophy wall.
Grats, {0}! Swing by the house and I'll add your name to the guestbook.

~ own_death
Ope. Down. Shoulda measured twice.
Ope. Well, that's a heck of a thing. Guess it's time for a hotdish when I get back.
Ope. Not on my floors, at least. The new planks are still too shiny to stain.

~ other_death
Oh, {0}! Okay. Deep breath. Let's get you back up, nice and easy.
Ope, {0}. Down, but not out. I'll have a warm bed ready at the house.
Ope, {0}. You should've worn gloves. It's a slippery world out there.
Ope, {0}. The floor's no place for you. Up and at 'em, now.

~ drop
{item}! That's going on the wall. I've got just the spot.
Got a spot on the trophy wall for {item}. Gerald will have company.
Ope, found {item}. Well made, that one. Built to last.
{item}, huh? That'd make a real nice housewarming gift for someone.

~ reply rvr
Sure thing, {0}. Just hope nobody messes with my place while I'm gone.

~ opener xp
Building a house, one board at a time. Same as levelling up.
Every board I nail down is another level under my belt. No shortcuts here.

~ opener zones
The view from {zone} is real nice, but the wind? Uff da, it likes to play tricks on ya.
{zone} is real nice, but I'd want to check the drainage first.

~ opener dungeons
Dungeons could use better lighting and a handrail.
Dungeons are fine for adventuring, but I'd never live in one. The damp would ruin my floors.

~ opener fun
Fixing the fence on a quiet Saturday, now that's my idea of fun.
A quiet barbecue with everyone sounds nice. No dying involved. Uff da.

~ opener questions
Anybody know a good way to keep moss off a roof? I've tried everything, but it keeps coming back.
Do you folks remember whose birthday is this week? I feel like it's somebody's.

~ opener classes
Every {class} should own a house, dontcha know. It settles you right down.

~ cheeky_reply banter [if tone_down off]
Ope! Well. Let's talk about my fence instead. It's really something, dontcha know.

~ reply thank
You betcha, {0}. That's what neighbours do.

~ reply dungeon
Let's go, {0}, but take it slow. Nobody needs a tumble in there.

~ reply grinding
Grinding's like mowing on a nice summer day, {0}. Takes a while, but it's steady work.

~ opener rvr
Well, now. I should be focused on the fight, but did I leave the stove on back home?

~ opener trading
I only buy things built to last, like a solid porch.

~ opener gripes
Ope. That neighbour's dog has been digging up my flower bed again. Real nice.



# Midgard: Barbalicious, Troll Savage, from Fort Atla. Big, rough, gentle underneath; house is a cosy hall in Jordheim housing.
=== midgard
~ ambient
Grew up in Fort Atla. Cold, windy, real nice. Built the hall with the door a little taller, though.
Hall's got a good fire going. Come on in, dontcha know. Duck at the door.
Got a boar's head over the hearth. Real nice. Its eyes follow you.
Big hands, small house. Ope, watch the mead cups.

~ opener realm
Jordheim housing's quiet. Bit of snow, bit of mead. Perfect.
Midgard has the best halls. Mine's the cosiest one.

~ reply greeting
Skol, {0}! Oh, you betcha, come see the hall!

~ drop
{item}! Over the hearth it goes. Next to the boar.

# Albion: Barbaliciouse, Inconnu Reaver, from Llyn Barfog. A bit dark and brooding, but invites tea; house in Albion housing.
=== albion
~ ambient
Grew up by Llyn Barfog. Misty lake, good fishing. The cottage has a lake view. A puddle view. Close enough.
Kettle's on, parlour's warm. Come on over, dontcha know.
Mounted a nice pair of antlers by the window. Ope, mind your head.
Nice cottage. Crooked chimney. Real nice, though.

~ opener realm
Camelot's housing is lovely. Neat hedges, nice neighbours.
Albion's got the best tea. And my parlour has the best chairs.

~ reply greeting
Well hello, {0}! You oughta come for tea. Oh, you betcha.

~ drop
{item}! For the parlour wall. Real nice.

# Hibernia: Barbalicioush, Firbolg Valewalker, from Mag Mell. Gentle and green, garden-minded; house in Hibernia housing.
=== hibernia
~ ambient
Grew up in Mag Mell. Everybody had a garden there. Mine's still the best one, dontcha know.
Garden's coming along real nice. Come see the roses. Dontcha know.
Put a stag's skull over the door. Gives the house character.
Ope, the moss is growing on the porch again. It's lovely.

~ opener realm
Tir na Nog housing is green and quiet. My kinda place.
Hibernia's got the best gardens. Mine's the best of those.

~ reply greeting
Hi there, {0}! Come see the garden, you betcha.

~ drop
{item}! For the hall by the garden. Real nice.
